{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02706",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.04,
      "end_seconds": 4.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.05,
      "end_seconds": 10.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.02,
      "end_seconds": 21.09,
      "duration_seconds": 9.07,
      "text": "So, I've been feeling sick, doctor. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.38,
      "end_seconds": 25.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.02,
      "end_seconds": 39.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.44,
      "end_seconds": 63.71,
      "duration_seconds": 13.27,
      "text": "Okay: temp 36.7 degrees, BP is 122 over 70, height 152 centimetres, respiratory rate 17, weight 66 kilos, pulse 84, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, BMI works out to 28.6."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.6,
      "end_seconds": 83.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.37,
      "end_seconds": 119.82,
      "duration_seconds": 35.45,
      "text": "Well, um, it's been going on for about a week. I did try to ignore it for a while. Oh, and severe pain in my left side going to the groin. That's been about the same, two days. Sorry, uh, what was I saying, I did have blood in the urine at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.0,
      "end_seconds": 123.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Okay, how about passing no urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.32,
      "end_seconds": 129.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Not that I've noticed, no passing no urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.92,
      "end_seconds": 135.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Right, have you noticed fever, burning when passing urine or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.32,
      "end_seconds": 138.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "No, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.54,
      "end_seconds": 143.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Okay, how are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.38,
      "end_seconds": 147.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.81,
      "end_seconds": 151.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.95,
      "end_seconds": 154.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.51,
      "end_seconds": 158.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.32,
      "end_seconds": 162.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Rosuvastatin. I take it at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.23,
      "end_seconds": 166.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.08,
      "end_seconds": 169.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "It's 10 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.73,
      "end_seconds": 173.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.22,
      "end_seconds": 179.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.24,
      "end_seconds": 182.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.7,
      "end_seconds": 187.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.83,
      "end_seconds": 190.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.98,
      "end_seconds": 193.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "No, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.33,
      "end_seconds": 212.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.0,
      "end_seconds": 218.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Walnuts. I come out in... well, hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.64,
      "end_seconds": 235.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.55,
      "end_seconds": 241.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "I have epilepsy, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.17,
      "end_seconds": 245.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Right, and anything else to add?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.61,
      "end_seconds": 248.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Yes, high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.99,
      "end_seconds": 256.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "So, yes, epilepsy and high cholesterol are known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.98,
      "end_seconds": 263.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.36,
      "end_seconds": 266.06,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.02,
      "end_seconds": 268.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.65,
      "end_seconds": 288.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "You are writhing in pain with tenderness in the left loin but your tummy is soft."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.57,
      "end_seconds": 315.55,
      "duration_seconds": 21.98,
      "text": "So, you can sit up now. Okay, so my impression is this: It's hard to say. Kidney stone colic is one possibility and a urine infection another, and I'd rather not commit yet. I want a CT scan of the kidneys and bladder done, that's for renal colic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 317.3,
      "end_seconds": 321.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "We have a slot Tuesday at 2 pm, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.82,
      "end_seconds": 346.14,
      "duration_seconds": 22.32,
      "text": "I'll start you on diclofenac, 75 milligrams, once now, single dose. That's for renal colic. Drink plenty of water and strain the urine to catch the stone. I'll also refer you to the urology clinic. Come back in one week. Right, is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.89,
      "end_seconds": 349.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}